<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shravanabelagola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shravanabelagola is a town in Hassan district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and one of the most important pilgrimage centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/digambara">Digambara</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jainism</a>. Tradition holds that the Maurya emperor Chandragupta and the monk Bhadrabahu ended their lives there. Its two hills hold temples and hundreds of inscriptions, and on Vindhyagiri stands the 17-metre statue of Bahubali, Gommateshwara, commissioned around 983 by the Western Ganga minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chavundaraya">Chavundaraya</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shravanabelagola.jpg" alt="Shravanabelagola" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ananth H V · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shravanabelagola_Hillview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
